Package: hd-kernel-server
Version: @META_DEB_VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: linux-image-@RELEASE@ (= @KERNEL_DEB_VERSION@),
 zfs-modules-@RELEASE@ (= @ZFS_DEB_VERSION@)
Conflicts: hd-kernel, hd-kernel-vm, hd-kernel-desktop, linux-image-amd64, linux-headers-amd64,
 linux-base-amd64, zfs-dkms
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Description: HyprDebian kernel for servers
 Depends on the most recent HyprDebian kernel for servers of @SUITE@ and its
 ZFS module, so that they are installed and upgraded with it. The kernel is
 that of hd-kernel, linux @KERNEL_VERSION@ of Debian with its patches and its
 config, but of the drivers only those of the hardware of servers and of
 software, and the targets of iSCSI, Fibre Channel and NVMe over TCP and Fibre
 Channel; the ZFS module is that of zfs-linux @ZFS_VERSION@, built against it.
 Both are built on the build server and signed with a key that is made for
 the build and thrown away, so a system needs neither DKMS nor a compiler for
 ZFS, and the kernel trusts no other key for its modules.
 .
 It replaces the kernel of Debian and the other HyprDebian kernels, and DKMS
 for ZFS: installing it removes hd-kernel, hd-kernel-vm, hd-kernel-desktop,
 linux-image-amd64, linux-headers-amd64, linux-base-amd64 and zfs-dkms, so DKMS
 builds no ZFS module that the kernel does not trust.
 See hd-kernel-server(7).
